<p class="home"><a href="index.html">← the ladder</a></p>
<h1 class="ttl">The Curriculum, Line by Line, in the Ladder's Language</h1>
<p>Rule (STRUCTURE, 2026-10-25): every line item of the school curriculum is named on the page that earns it, under its school name as well as the ladder's own, and proved there rather than handed over. A missing item is a gap in the plan, to be placed, not skipped.</p>
<p><strong>Benchmarks.</strong> Rungs 0–30 (the first five years): the Common Core high school standards, AP Precalculus, AP Calculus AB/BC, AP Statistics, SAT and ACT math. The science annexes: NGSS high school, AP Physics 1, 2, C: Mechanics, C: E&amp;M, AP Chemistry, AP Biology, AP Environmental Science, AP Computer Science A and Principles. Past rung 30: MIT, Stanford, Cambridge and Oxford, undergraduate core through PhD qualifying level, in mathematics and in the math-heavy sciences.</p>
<p><strong>Status.</strong> <em>earned</em>: a built page teaches or proves it (checked by searching the page). <em>planned</em>: only a planned row covers it. <em>beyond</em>: only in the far-future list. <em>missing</em>: no row covers it. <em>out of scope</em>: not built on mathematics (lab work, descriptive biology, Java syntax).</p>
