</ul><section class="cw" id="ccss_hs"><h2>Common Core high school</h2><p>Source: Common Core State Standards for Mathematics, High School, from the official site, thecorestandards.org (https://thecorestandards.org/Math/Content/HSN/, /HSA/, /HSF/, /HSG/, /HSS/, /HSM/; one page per domain, e.g. https://thecorestandards.org/Math/Content/HSA/REI/). Codes are given in the site's form, with the <code>CCSS.Math.Content.</code> prefix dropped (HSN.RN.A.1 is the N-RN.1 of the printed standards). Line items are paraphrases, not quotations. "Earned" means a built page teaches or proves it, checked by searching that page's text; "planned" means only a planned row covers it; "missing" means no row does. When a line item has a required part that is still only planned, it is marked planned and the Note says which part is already earned.</p>
