<h3>Missing items and where they would fit</h3>
<p><strong>AP Precalculus</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Polar graphs (3.14, 3.15): add to 21i (Around the circle) or a 21 tech row on r = f(θ); rates of r against θ belong there too.</li>
<li>Parametric functions (4.1–4.3, 4.7): a new 18 tech row (curves traced over time), with 21b supplying (cos t, sin t).</li>
<li>Vector-valued functions (4.9): extend 27a with arrows that move in time.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>AP Calculus AB and BC</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Slope fields (7.3, 7.4): add to 24c (Euler's method): the field is the picture Euler steps through.</li>
<li>Average value of a function (8.1): add to 16g; also pays off 14c (MVT for integrals).</li>
<li>Arc length (8.13, 9.3): add to 21o (Adding up slices) or 21n; 29b's ds² looks back on it.</li>
<li>Parametric calculus (9.1–9.3, 9.6): a new 21 tech row (motion along a curve), after parametrised circles in 21b.</li>
<li>Vector-valued calculus (9.4–9.6): a tech row at 27 or 28 (differentiate and integrate arrows component-wise).</li>
<li>Polar area (9.8, 9.9): a 21 tech row after polar graphs (½∫r² dθ from sector areas).</li>
<li>Integral test, p-series and harmonic series (10.4, 10.5): add to 22b; needs rung 16's improper integrals.</li>
<li>Alternating series test, absolute vs conditional convergence (10.7, 10.9): add to 22b.</li>
<li>Alternating series error bound (10.10): add to 23b alongside the Lagrange remainder.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>AP Statistics</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Variables and one-variable displays (1.1–1.6, 1.8, 1.9): a new data-description support row at 30 (or a 5 support row: tables, bar charts, histograms, boxplots, median and quartiles need only fractions and order).</li>
<li>Data collection, sampling bias, experimental design (1.10, 1.12, 1.13): a new 30 tech row on designing studies, before 30e.</li>
<li>Two-way tables (2.1): add to 30a with conditional probability.</li>
<li>Simulation (2.3): a 30 tech row, or 30·comp (random numbers by hand and by machine).</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>SAT Math (digital SAT)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Evaluating statistical claims: observational studies vs experiments: the same new study-design row at 30 suggested for AP Statistics.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>ACT Math (enhanced ACT)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Data collection methods: the same new study-design row at 30.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Thin spots inside planned rows</h3>
<p>Rows that cover a topic only in part, worth widening when they are built:</p>
<ul>
<li>22b lists geometric, comparison and ratio tests only; the nth-term test (10.3) needs naming.</li>
<li>30f plans χ² goodness of fit on Mendel's counts. AP dropped goodness of fit in the fall 2026 revision and kept χ² for homogeneity and independence (3.14, 3.15). 30e and 30f don't name the t distribution, Type I/II errors or power.</li>
<li>Median, quartiles and boxplots appear nowhere (grep finds only 'mediant' in 5h). SAT, ACT and AP Statistics 1.7–1.8 all need them.</li>
<li>20i (Moving graphs) is the only row for function transformations (Precalculus 1.12, ACT). 9e has only the a·x² stretch.</li>
<li>21o (Adding up slices) has no brief yet. This crosswalk assumes it covers volumes by cross-section, disc and washer (Calculus 8.7–8.12).</li>
<li>Solid geometry (surface area and volume of prisms, cylinders, cones, spheres) has no explicit row. 18f covers plane Euclid.</li>
<li>Linear inequalities in two variables (half-planes) aren't covered. 8g is one variable only.</li>
</ul>
