<li>AP Calculus AB/BC CED and fall 2026 clarifications: https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/ap-calculus-ab-and-bc-course-and-exam-description.pdf , https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/ap-calculus-ab-bc-course-and-exam-description-clarifications-effective-fall-2026.pdf</li>
<li>AP Statistics CED effective fall 2026: https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/ap-statistics-course-and-exam-description-effective-fall-2026.pdf ; course page https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/courses/ap-statistics/course ; topic titles for 4.3–5.5 cross-checked at https://num8ers.com/guides/ap-statistics-syllabus-2026-vs-2020/ and the Math Medic CED alignment</li>
<li>SAT: https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/k12-educators/about/alignment/math/psat-10-psat-nmsqt-sat , https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/sat/whats-on-the-test/math/overview</li>
<li>ACT: https://act.org/content/act/en/products-and-services/the-act/test-preparation/description-of-math-test.html</li>
</ul></section><section class="cw" id="science"><h2>NGSS and the AP sciences and computing</h2><h3>Science and computing crosswalk: NGSS high school and AP sciences</h3>
<p>Section of the curriculum crosswalk for The Ladder. It covers the science and computing curricula the STEM annexes should meet, from high school through AP.</p>
<p><strong>Status key.</strong>
- <strong>earned</strong>: a built row of LADDER_ROWS.tsv covers it. Each was checked by grepping that row's HTML file.
- <strong>planned</strong>: only planned rows cover it. Most planned annexes have a title and no brief, so the match goes by title.
- <strong>missing</strong>: a math-driven annex should cover it, and no row does.
- <strong>out of scope</strong>: the content is descriptive, lab-procedural, about one language or about society, not built on math.</p>
<p>Page labels follow the ladder: <code>13·phys</code> is an annex, <code>13k</code> a math page, <code>9·cb4</code> a call-back. The only files counted are those LADDER_ROWS.tsv lists. The Thompson "Calculus Bites" pages and the Spivak pages (bite<em>, s</em>, t*, old.html) in the same folder are not ladder rows and were ignored.</p>
<p><strong>Sources and access.</strong> The proxy blocked direct downloads, so every list was read through a fetcher from official pages:
- NGSS codes and statements: nextgenscience.org topic and DCI arrangement pages.
- AP units and topics: the current Course and Exam Description PDFs on apcentral.collegeboard.org.</p>
<p>The fetcher's text was incomplete in three places:
- AP Physics 1, Unit 7: no topic list came through.
- AP Chemistry, topics 3.7, 3.10, 3.11 and 3.13.
- Ten AP Environmental Science topics.</p>
<p>Those gaps are filled from the previous edition of the same CED and flagged † in the tables. All line items are paraphrases, not quotations.</p>
<hr />
<h2>1. NGSS high school performance expectations</h2>
<p>Sources: https://www.nextgenscience.org/dci-arrangement/hs-ps1-matter-and-its-interactions, https://www.nextgenscience.org/node/1075 (PS2), https://nextgenscience.org/node/1104 (PS3), https://www.nextgenscience.org/node/1060 (PS4), https://nextgenscience.org/hsls1-molecules-organisms-structures-processes, https://nextgenscience.org/node/1061 (LS2), https://www.nextgenscience.org/dci-arrangement/hs-ls3-heredity-inheritance-and-variation-traits, https://nextgenscience.org/dci-arrangement/hs-ls4-biological-evolution-unity-and-diversity, https://www.nextgenscience.org/node/1056 (ESS1), https://www.nextgenscience.org/topic-arrangement/hsearths-systems (ESS2), https://nextgenscience.org/dci-arrangement/hs-ess3-earth-and-human-activity, https://nextgenscience.org/node/953 (ETS1)</p>
<p>The fetched pages did not list four groups of codes: LS2-3/4/5, ESS1-1 to 1-4, ESS2-4 and ETS1-2/3/4. Those are paraphrased from the published NGSS set.</p>
